Certainly! Below is a complete, production-ready `package.json` file for the backend of a MERN stack calculator application. This file includes necessary dependencies, scripts, and metadata.

{
  "name": "calculator-backend",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Backend for a calculator application built using the MERN stack.",
  "main": "server.js",
  "scripts": {
    "start": "node server.js",
    "dev": "nodemon server.js",
    "lint": "eslint.",
    "test": "jest",
    "test:watch": "jest --watch",
    "coverage": "jest --coverage"
  },
  "repository": {
    "type": "git",
    "url": "git+https://github.com/yourusername/app-backend.git"
  },
  "keywords": [
    "mern",
    "calculator",
    "backend",
    "nodejs",
    "express"
  ],
  "author": "Your Name",
  "license": "MIT",
  "bugs": {
    "url": "https://github.com/yourusername/app-backend/issues"
  },
  "homepage": "https://github.com/yourusername/app-backend#readme",
  "dependencies": {
    "express": "^4.17.1",
    "mongoose": "^5.10.0",
    "morgan": "^1.10.0"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "eslint": "^7.24.0",
    "jest": "^26.6.3",
    "nodemon": "^2.0.7"
  },
  "engines": {
    "node": ">=12.0.0"
  }
}

### Explanation:

- **name**: The name of your package, `calculator-backend`.
- **version**: The current version of your package, `1.0.0`.
- **description**: A short description of what your package does.
- **main**: The entry point of your application, `server.js`.
- **scripts**:
  - `start`: Starts the application using `node server.js`.
  - `dev`: Starts the application in development mode using `nodemon`.
  - `lint`: Lints the project using ESLint.
  - `test`: Runs the test suite using Jest.
  - `test:watch`: Runs the test suite in watch mode.
  - `coverage`: Generates a test coverage report.
- **repository**: Information about the repository where the code is hosted.
- **keywords**: Keywords that describe your project.
- **author**: The author of the project.
- **license**: The license under which your project is distributed, in this case, MIT.
- **bugs**: URL to the issue tracker.
- **homepage**: URL to the project’s homepage.
- **dependencies**:
  - `express`: Web framework for Node.js.
  - `mongoose`: ODM (Object Data Modeling) library for MongoDB and Node.js.
  - `morgan`: HTTP request logger middleware for Node.js.
- **devDependencies**:
  - `eslint`: Tool for identifying and reporting on patterns found in ECMAScript/JavaScript code.
  - `jest`: Delightful JavaScript Testing.
  - `nodemon`: Tool that helps develop node.js based applications by automatically restarting the node application when file changes in the directory are detected.
- **engines**: Specifies the version of Node.js required to run this project.

Make sure to replace placeholders like `yourusername` and `Your Name` with your actual GitHub username and name.